From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: The shell hears of a window that goes, hidden or not.

HSHELL_WINDOWDESTROYED went out only for a window still visible when it was
destroyed. The taskbar learns of windows by the shell hook and also by
enumerating them (RefreshWindowList, when an unknown window takes the
foreground; the foreground timer), so it could hold the button of a window
that was hidden first and destroyed later, or that became visible by its
style without SWP_SHOWWINDOW: the button outlived the window, one more after
every failed start of a program (EffectCraft: its window, a message box, gone,
and an "EffectCraft" button left). win32k tells the shell of every toplevel
window without an owner that is destroyed; so does the server now. A button
the taskbar does not have is ignored there.
---
diff --git a/server/window.c b/server/window.c
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -2306,7 +2306,10 @@

     assert( win->handle );
     composition_changed( win );
-    if (is_visible( win ) && is_shell_hook_window( win ))
+    /* Arctic: as win32k, the shell hears of every toplevel window that goes,
+       shown or hidden: the taskbar finds windows by enumerating them too, and
+       one destroyed hidden stayed there as the button of nothing */
+    if (is_shell_hook_window( win ))
         shell_hook_notify( win->desktop, HSHELL_WINDOWDESTROYED, win->handle );

     /* hide the window */
